1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,000
WHO ROUTES THE AGENTS?

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:12,500
One team finds a person can
usually follow 3 to 5 sessions.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,000
YOU DO.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
THE SUPER-AGENT DESIGN
from DeepSeek's Harness team

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
TWO LEVELS · A DESIGN, NOT A PRODUCT

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
ONE LONG-LIVED ROUTER

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
IT ROUTES. IT NEVER EXECUTES.
Whole tasks go down, unsplit.

8
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:38,250
PROTOTYPE ROUTER:
KEEPS A SHELL, NO WRITE TOOLS

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,500
A WORKER: ITS OWN CONTEXT
One task. Full tools.

10
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:47,250
By design, only the Router answers you.

11
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
ONE ROUTER FOR ALL THIS?

12
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,500
EVENTS, NOT JUST PROMPTS

13
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,500
GATE ONE: PLAIN CODE
No model runs.

14
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:01,000
THEN A MODEL JUDGES.

15
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:04,500
PROTOTYPE DEFAULT:
UNASKED WORK IS ONLY RECORDED

16
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,000
1. FEW REACH THE ROUTER.

17
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,000
FOLLOW-UPS GO STRAIGHT IN
Seen by the Router. Not decided.

18
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:14,000
CHEAPER, NOT FASTER

19
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,500
~27% fewer tokens than without it
AUTHORS' TEST

20
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:20,000
2. FOLLOW-UPS SKIP ITS DECISION.

21
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,000
ARRIVALS WAIT,
THEN ENTER TOGETHER

22
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,000
6.4 s → 1.6 s model time per decision,
at ~40× the load (authors' stress test)

23
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,000
AUTHORS' STRESS TEST · MOCK WORKERS

24
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,500
UP TO A LIMIT PER CALL.

25
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:38,000
3. THE REST ARRIVE TOGETHER.

26
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:43,000
ITS CONTEXT IS A CACHE
What it needs soon stays in view.

27
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:47,000
BY DESIGN: RECALL BY ID
It loses less. Not nothing.

28
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,500
4. DETAILS WAIT BEHIND IDS.

29
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:54,000
THE AUTHORS' TEST
Synthetic. 5 runs. Indicative only.

30
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:59,000
SUPER-AGENT vs ONE SESSION + SUBAGENT TOOL
(the session was told to delegate first)

31
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:03,000
SLOWEST TASKS: ABOUT HALF THE TIME
P95 · RE-PLOTTED

32
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:06,000
TYPICAL TASKS: ABOUT 10% FASTER
P50

33
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:10,500
THE PRICE: 2–4× THE TOKENS of one session
(told to delegate first · left to choose)

34
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:15,000
PROPOSED: Running in the cloud.
A check for stuck Workers.

35
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:19,500
OPEN: Long memory. Security.
Stepping in mid-task. More Routers.

36
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,000
WHO ROUTES THE AGENTS?

37
